Z||000000||chris6878||06-29-2000||02:33 AM||||hey...<P>The last time i had my car jacked up when i was working it, i noticed some slack in the front drivers tire. I can press against the front of the tire and it will tild in a bit. Something clicks when i do this. I dont think this is normal..  at least i hope not...     i drive this car 80+ miles a day to work. When i reach speed around 60 or higher my car tends to vibrate or shake kinda.. and i can definitely fill the slack  (or whatever it is) in the steering whell on hard turns... <P>what would this be? (i havent worked on the front end of a fiero before) so i dont have a clue whats happening up there...<P>TIA,<BR>chris   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-29-2000||02:38 AM||||Does it tilt top and bottom or does it tilt side by side? Top to bottom is bad ball joint(s). Side to side is bad tierod.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-29-2000||09:18 AM||||If it falls off, you need lugnuts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||06-29-2000||01:40 PM||||have someone else move the wheel while you watch from under. sounds like it could be either a ball joint or wheel bearing. likely a ball joint. you should be able to see one or both move if there is visible play in the tire. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||06-29-2000||02:27 PM||||side to side is the movement... and yes the lug nuts are tight..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>thanx guys..<BR>chris||||reg||3
